      "line_no": 1,
      "code": "INSERT INTO Students(sid, name, login, age, gpa)",
      "explanation": "'INTO' clause which is mantantory in 'INSERT' clause is to specify the table and columns to store data. The order of inserted data should be matched with the order of each column specified in SQL statement. If the column names are omitted, the data are inserted by the column order of table definition."
    },
    {
      "line_no": 2,
      "code": "      VALUES('53688', 'Smith', 'smith@ee', 18, 3.2);",
      "explanation": "'VALUES' keyword is necessary to define the inserted data. The value for sid, name, or login whose domain types are character is surrounded by single quotation mark."
    }
  ],
